\pard\sa160\sl259\slmult0\tx1630\ul\b\fs28 ADDRESSING MODES:\par
\ulnone\b0 Addressing mode refers to the topic, that how we access different registers and the data stored in them.\par
\ul\b TYPES OF ADDRESSING MODES:\par
\ulnone\b0 There are three types of addressing modes:\par
\ul\b 1.Register Addressing:\par
\ulnone\b0 When both operands are registers.\par
\ul\b Example:\ulnone\b0 Add dl,dl\par
\ul\b 2.Immediate Addressing:\par
\ulnone\b0 When one operand is register and other operand is constant\par
\ul\b Example:\ulnone\b0 Add dl,2\par
\ul\b 3.Memory Addressing:\par
\ulnone\b0 When one operand is register and other operand is saved in the memory\par
\ul\b EXAMPLE:\ulnone\b0  Add al,[num]\par

